    "id": "p34-q06-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "The coefficient of $x^5$ in $(ax^2+ax+3)(2+x)^6$ is 476.\n\nFind the value of $a$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=2$\n\nMatch the $x^3$, $x^4$ and $x^5$ terms of $(2+x)^6$ with the three terms of the first factor.",
      "worked": "In $(2+x)^6$, the coefficients needed are\n$$\\begin{align*}[x^3](2+x)^6&=\\binom{6}{3}2^3=160\\\\{}[x^4](2+x)^6&=\\binom{6}{4}2^2=60\\\\{}[x^5](2+x)^6&=\\binom{6}{5}2=12\\end{align*}$$\nMatch $ax^2$ with $x^3$, $ax$ with $x^4$, and $3$ with $x^5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}[x^5](ax^2+ax+3)(2+x)^6&=160a+60a+3(12)\\\\{}[x^5](ax^2+ax+3)(2+x)^6&=220a+36\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}220a+36&=476\\\\220a&=440\\\\a&=2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
